cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Congro;Library in academic or technical work, please cite this repository."
title: "Congro;Library"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vinicios"
    given-names: "Samuel"
    alias: "okarin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/samucaoo1/Congro-Library"
url: "https://github.com/samucaoo1/Congro-Library"
license: "EUPL-1.2"
abstract: >-
  Congro;Library is a modular C11 library for portable systems programming,
  education, experimentation, and reusable low-level components. It includes
  facilities for memory, preprocessing, containers, concurrency, networking,
  chronometry, random generation, mathematics, text and Unicode processing,
  bit operations, reusable structures, and generic typed operations.
keywords:
  - C11
  - C library
  - systems programming
  - portable C
  - containers
  - concurrency
  - networking
  - Unicode
  - metaprogramming
  - educational software
